{
  "corpus_version": "engineering-assurance.compatibility-corpus/v1",
  "purpose": "The accepted fixture set for the contract campaign. Every legacy case is real bytes or a single named mutation of real bytes; every producer case is a real producer's own output. Nothing here is a verdict, and nothing here is executed.",
  "limitations": [
    "Legacy PGM-01 history in this ecosystem is entirely v1 and records only pass, skipped, and inconclusive. The failed, unavailable, not-computed, stale, and tampered cases are therefore derived, and each one records the exact edit that produced it.",
    "PGM-01 v1 has no not-computed status. The mapping refuses one rather than translating it; not-computed reaches the shared model through a current-model producer record.",
    "No real PGM-01 v2 record exists to retain, so the v2 case is built on the constructed v2 fixture and is labelled as constructed.",
    "Retaining these bytes proves fixture integrity and mapping behaviour offline. It does not re-observe the source repositories."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
